title: "Structural Recognition above Metric Similarity (SRMS): From Recognition-Gated Cosine Scoring to Recognition-Centered AI"

type: article

version: 1.0.0

date-released: 2026-07-13

authors:

* family-names: Tan
  given-names: Sizhe
* name: GPT-Obot

abstract: >-
Structural Recognition above Metric Similarity (SRMS) presents a
recognition-centered computational architecture for future AI. It argues
that structural identity, critical deltas, decision boundaries, runtime
activation, runtime invariants, structural confidence, and certified
structural assets should be established before metric similarity performs
ranking and optimization. The repository introduces the Base-Delta
Asymmetry Principle, Recognition-Gated Cosine Scoring, Small but Decisive
Structural Deltas, Structural Recognition as Runtime Intelligence,
Structural Confidence Accumulation, Certified Structural Components, and
the Structural Recognition Pipeline for Future AI. Its central principle
is that recognition establishes the computational world, while similarity
optimizes inside that world.

